00:00:24.722 --> 00:00:26.180
ALEX BUTNAREANU:
Encryption at rest

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.502
is central to our
security strategy,

00:00:28.502 --> 00:00:30.710
and there are several options
based on the customer's

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:31.970
security needs.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:35.870
By default, data at rest is
encrypted in all Google Cloud

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.430
Platform products.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:40.520
For certain classes of data or
where you have a requirement

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.460
to manage your
encryption key, we

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.900
give customers the option
of managing their own keys

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.140
using Customer-Managed
Encryption Keys, or CMEC

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:52.220
for short, using a managed
service called Cloud KMS.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.393
Then, for a small
percentage of workloads,

00:00:54.393 --> 00:00:56.810
there may be a requirement to
generate your own encryption

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.620
key or manage it on premise.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.170
And for that we
provide the option

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.860
to use Customer-Supplied
Encryption Keys, or CSEC

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:04.840
for short.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.770
Let's see how this works.

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:10.160
By default, when I upload
a file to cloud storage,

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.320
it will automatically
be encrypted at rest

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:19.120
with Google-managed
keys, as we can see here.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.030
This is transparent
to the user, but a lot

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.680
happens behind the scenes.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.480
Data's split into
chunks, and each chunk

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.300
is encrypted with a unique
data encryption key.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.400
Then these data
encryption keys are

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.250
encrypted with their
own key encryption keys,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.930
stored in Google's KMS.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.310
The data chunks are then
distributed across Google Cloud

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:39.870
Storage systems and replicated
in encrypted form for backup

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.320
and disaster recovery.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.680
And this happens in real
time, all by default

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.283
and transparent to the user.

00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:46.950
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
Well, that's a relief.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.110
But, like, I still have
